[
{"claim": "A finished detached build stage looked running forever because run_stage never wait()ed on its setsid child: the zombie kept its /proc/<pid> entry, so every existence-based liveness check (builder_status, stage_log, stop_build, run_stage's already-running guard) read it as alive and blocked the next stage. Fixed: run_stage spawns a reaper thread that wait()s the child, and all liveness checks read the state field from /proc/<pid>/stat, treating state Z as not-running.", "detail": "General lesson beyond this control: /proc/<pid> existing does not mean the process is running - a zombie of your own process keeps the entry until reaped. Any spawner that records a detached child's pid must either wait() it (reaper thread) or check /proc/<pid>/stat state, not directory existence. Verified live: builder_status flipped to not-running immediately after the patch, and the extract stage completed with the pid fully reaped.", "tags": "agent.browser_builder,zombie,proc,liveness,process-management,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787767298932},
{"claim": "mach bootstrap is a dead end for the Noobscape deps stage and is not needed: the kit's mozconfig omits --enable-bootstrap, so mach build uses system toolchains - skip the deps stage and install prerequisites directly (apt: clang/llvm, nodejs, nasm, and the -dev headers for gtk-3, dbus-glib-1, x11-xcb, pulse, xt; cbindgen installs without root via cargo install).", "detail": "Three independent bootstrap failures found 2026-08-26: (1) --no-interactive is a GLOBAL mach flag that must precede the subcommand - trailing it exits 1 with 'unrecognized argument' (fixed in build.sh, workspace copy and shipped kit asset); (2) bootstrap runs sudo apt-get, which needs a password no detached stage can supply; (3) its toolchain fetch crashes on release source tarballs with the known 'python/mozboot/**/*android* did not match anything' bug, downloading nothing into ~/.mozbuild. The glean-sdk wheel failure in the same log is cosmetic (telemetry only; mach continues without it). After system packages exist, run the build stage directly - it re-runs configure itself, and configure names any still-missing -dev package precisely early in the log.", "tags": "agent.browser_builder,firefox,mach,bootstrap,deps,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787767303797},
{"end": true}]
